  "text_input": "Patient was in his usual state of health when 2 days back during the morning while praying, he suddenly developed weakness of right arm which was characterised by sudden loss and inability to hold any object or raise his arm for a period of 5-10 minutes. No other symptoms such as loss of consciousness, slurring of speech, deviation of angle of mouth or involuntary passage of urine. Patient came to KIMS OPD the following day where he had a similar episode, this time affecting both right arm and right leg. It was characterised by inability to raise his right leg or to support any weight and hence being unable to stand. This was associated with slurring of speech. This episode lasted 5-10 minutes before completely resolving.",
